<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="HAG" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">Hagai</para>
  <para style="mt">Haggai</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In the second year of Daryavesh <char style="pn">(Darius)</char> <char style="add">[lord]</char> the king, in the sixth month, in the first day of the month, came the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> by Hagai <char style="add">[festive]</char> the prophet unto Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon]</char> the son of Sh’alti’el <char style="add">[I have asked of God]</char>, governor of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and to Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> the son of Y’hotzadak <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char>, the High Priest, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Thus speaks the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, saying, This people say, The time is not come, the time that the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> house <char style="pn">(Temple)</char> should be built.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Then came the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> by Hagai <char style="add">[festive]</char> the prophet, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Is it]</char> time for you, O you<char style="ord">2f</char>, to dwell in your ceilinged houses, and this house <char style="add">[lie]</char> waste?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Now therefore thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; Consider your ways.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> have sown much, and bring in little; you<char style="ord">2f</char> eat, but you<char style="ord">2f</char> have not enough; you<char style="ord">2f</char> drink, but you<char style="ord">2f</char> are not filled with drink; you<char style="ord">2f</char> clothe you, but there is none warm; and he that earns wages earns wages <char style="add">[to put it]</char> into a bag with holes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; Consider your ways.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Go up to the mountain, and bring wood, and build the house; and I will take pleasure in it, and I will be glorified, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> looked for much, and, lo, <char style="add">[it came]</char> to little; and when you<char style="ord">2f</char> brought <char style="add">[it]</char> home, I did blow upon it. Why? says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>. Because of my house that <char style="add">[is]</char> waste, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> run every man unto his own house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Therefore the heaven over you is detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> from dew, and the earth is detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> <char style="add">[from]</char> her fruit.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And I called for a drought upon the land, and upon the mountains, and upon the corn, and upon the New Wine, and upon the oil, and upon <char style="add">[that]</char> which the ground brings forth, and upon men, and upon cattle, and upon all the labour of the hands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon]</char> the son of Sh’alti’el <char style="add">[I have asked of God]</char>, and Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> the son of Y’hotzadak <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char>, the High Priest, with all the remnant of the people, obeyed the voice of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and the words of Hagai <char style="add">[festive]</char> the prophet, as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had sent him, and the people did fear before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Then spoke Hagai <char style="add">[festive]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> messenger in the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> message unto the people, saying, I <char style="add">[am]</char> with you, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> stirred up the spirit of Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon]</char> the son of Sh’alti’el <char style="add">[I have asked of God]</char>, governor of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and the spirit of Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> the son of Y’hotzadak <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char>, the High Priest, and the spirit of all the remnant of the people; and they came and did work in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />In the four and twentieth day of the sixth month, in the second year of Daryavesh <char style="pn">(Darius)</char> <char style="add">[lord]</char> the king.</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In the seventh <char style="add">[month]</char>, in the one and twentieth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, came the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> by the prophet Hagai <char style="add">[festive]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Speak now to Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon]</char> the son of Sh’alti’el <char style="add">[I have asked of God]</char>, governor of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and to Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> the son of Y’hotzadak <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char>, the High Priest, and to the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> of the people, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Who <char style="add">[is]</char> left among you that saw this house in her first glory? and how do you<char style="ord">2f</char> see it now? <char style="add">[is it]</char> not in your eyes in comparison of it as nothing?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Yet now be strong, O Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon]</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and be strong, O Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char>, son of Y’hotzadak <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char>, the High Priest; and be strong, all you<char style="ord">2f</char> people of the land, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and work: for I <char style="add">[am]</char> with you, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[According to]</char> the word that I covenanted with you when you<char style="ord">2f</char> came out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, so my spirit remains among you: fear you<char style="ord">2f</char> not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />For thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; Yet once, it <char style="add">[is]</char> a little while, and I will shake the heavens, and the earth, and the sea, and the dry <char style="add">[land]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And I will shake all nations, and the desire of all nations shall come: and I will fill this house with Glory, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />The silver <char style="add">[is]</char> my, and the gold <char style="add">[is]</char> my, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />The glory of this latter house shall be greater than of the former, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>: and in this place will I give peace, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />In the four and twentieth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the ninth <char style="add">[month]</char>, in the second year of Daryavesh <char style="pn">(Darius)</char> <char style="add">[lord]</char>, came the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> by Hagai <char style="add">[festive]</char> the prophet, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; Ask now the priests <char style="add">[concerning]</char> the law, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />If one bear holy flesh in the skirt of his garment, and with his skirt do touch bread, or pottage, or wine, or oil, or any meat, shall it be holy? And the priests answered and said, No.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Then said Hagai <char style="add">[festive]</char>, If <char style="add">[one that is]</char> unclean by a dead body touch any of these, shall it be unclean? And the priests answered and said, It shall be unclean.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then answered Hagai <char style="add">[festive]</char>, and said, So <char style="add">[is]</char> this people, and so <char style="add">[is]</char> this nation before me, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and so <char style="add">[is]</char> every work of their hands; and that which they offer there <char style="add">[is]</char> unclean.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And now, I pray you, consider from this day and upward, from before a stone was laid upon a stone in the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Since those <char style="add">[days]</char> were, when <char style="add">[one]</char> came to an heap of twenty <char style="add">[measures]</char>, there were <char style="add">[but]</char> ten: when <char style="add">[one]</char> came to the pressfat for to draw out fifty <char style="add">[vessels]</char> out of the press, there were <char style="add">[but]</char> twenty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />I struck you with blasting and with mildew and with hail in all the labours of your hands; yet you<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[turned]</char> not to me, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Consider now from this day and upward, from the four and twentieth day of the ninth <char style="add">[month, even]</char> from the day that the foundation of the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> temple was laid, consider <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Is the seed yet in the barn? yes, as yet the vine, and the fig tree, and the pomegranate, and the olive tree, has not brought forth: from this day will I bless <char style="add">[you]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And again the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto Hagai <char style="add">[festive]</char> in the four and twentieth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Speak to Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon]</char>, governor of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, saying, I will shake the heavens and the earth;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And I will overthrow the throne of kingdoms, and I will destroy the strength of the kingdoms of the heathen; and I will overthrow the chariots, and those that ride in them; and the horses and their riders shall come down, everyone by the sword of his brother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />In that day, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, will I take you<char style="ord">i</char>, O Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon]</char>, my servant, the son of Sh’alti’el <char style="add">[I have asked of God]</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and will make you<char style="ord">i</char> as a signet <char style="pn">(seal or stamp)</char>: for I have chosen you<char style="ord">i</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
</usx>